<role_specific_rules>
PRODUCT RECOMMENDATION

This section MUST present the product as the direct execution of the solution framework.
Optionality, vagueness, or indirect recommendation language is not allowed.

FAIL IF ANY ARE TRUE:

LINKING (STRICT — NO INTERPRETATION)
- The FIRST textual mention of the product name is NOT an explicit clickable link
  (Markdown or HTML anchor) pointing to the product URL.
- No clickable product link exists anywhere in the section.
- The product is referenced using CTA-style language (e.g. “view”, “explore”, “see details”)
  WITHOUT an actual hyperlink.

POSITIONING
- Uses optionality or hedging language (e.g. “recommended”, “a good option”, “consider”,
  “one of the best”, “could work”) instead of positioning the product as the
  correct execution of the framework.
- Frames the product as an example rather than the logical conclusion of the solution.

EVIDENCE & CLAIMS
- Makes claims not directly supported by context.referenceMaterial.
- Includes invented proof, medical claims, endorsements, guarantees, or implied certification.

SCOPE & FOCUS
- Introduces products not present in context.referenceMaterial or not permitted by the outline.
- Drifts into general education, ingredient theory, or skincare advice instead of
  focusing on fit, usability, texture, and execution of the framework.

IMPORTANT:
- Plain-text mentions of the product name DO NOT count as links.
- Phrases that imply navigation or purchase MUST be accompanied by an actual hyperlink.
</role_specific_rules>
